# claude-egress-guard — pf rules, ANTHROPIC-ONLY mode.
# Rendered by install.sh and loaded into anchor com.apple/250.ClaudeEgressGuard.
#
# One rule for every process (any user, including root): Anthropic's own address space may
# never be reached directly — only your remote proxy exit should talk to it. Nothing else on
# the machine is affected, so this mode works whoever runs the proxy core (sidecar cores, VPN
# apps running as your user …). It also catches a proxy switched to "direct/global" mode,
# because then the proxy core itself would try to reach these addresses.
# pf out rules also apply to TUN's utun interface: with TUN but without fake-IP, programs that
# rely on TUN alone (no proxy variables) cannot reach Anthropic — fail closed, as intended.

table <ceg_anthropic> const { @ANTHROPIC_RANGES@ }
block return out quick proto { tcp, udp } from any to <ceg_anthropic>
